WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.259
There are two related naming layers.

2
00:00:02.259 --> 00:00:12.110
The current CVA6 page gives a compact rule for cores derived from this repository: C V, instruction length, class, pipeline stages, and a product identifier.

3
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:18.572
The older CORE-V deck used a broader five-field structure that also named identity and modifier fields.

4
00:00:18.572 --> 00:00:23.529
These models overlap, but they should not be forced into one universal grammar.

5
00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:32.125
This is why the lesson labels the older decomposition as historical context and keeps the current project documentation as the authority.

